{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:9291b71d89870432","name":"BD-3000 Luxury Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-9291b71d89870432","title":"BD-3000 Luxury Droid","revision":25153,"timestamp":"2024-11-13T15:20:14Z","sha256":"2a23e02bf2170cf28fc862ac6eeac3c6bddcf15f5cae4f5b391fb6fa98a83ac5","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25153","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=BD-3000%20Luxury%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-9291b71d89870432","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The BD-3000 by LeisureMech Enterprises is a serviceable Protocol Droid that can also be programmed to cook, do food service, pilot private repulsor yachts or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"},", do tailoring, handle light administrative duties, or even serve as a nanny or (with some modification) a bodyguard. Although the Droid has the capacity to speak more than a million languages and is programmed with knowledge of diplomatic ceremonies, the primary focus of the BD-3000 is to be aesthetic and complimentary. As a result, the Droids were extremely popular with Senators of the Republic, and with the wealthy who wanted to be seen as extravagant.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A large part of the extremely high price for BD Droids comes from the customized choice of shape, coloration, voice tone, and personality a customer can specify when ordering. Because of this customization, their used value is significantly lower than that of most other Droids (since custom options can't be changed). As a result, when an owner no longer has any use for a BD-3000 (because it's out of date, or the owner's tastes have changed, or a newer model has come out, or the owner has been imprisoned by the Empire), the Droid is often just junked or sold for parts.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["However, the Droids are no less functional for their lack of prestige. Criminal elements often buy or steal just-abandoned Luxury Droids for their own uses. Some are turned into Assassin Droids, and many are simply used as fancy Protocol Droids (although only a new BD-3000 is a symbol of status among the upper crust of society, any model is a sign of success for a crime lord). Others are radically modified and put to seedier uses (the addition of articulated lekku is fairly common, for example). Such criminal purposes are easier to arrange with BD-3000 Droids, because their core programming outlaws fewer activities (they are not forbidden to impersonate deities, for example), and they come equipped with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heuristic Processors"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heuristic_Processors"}," (to better anticipate their owners' preferences).\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["BD-3000 Luxury Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["BD-3000 Luxury Droid Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["3rd-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/3rd-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -1; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Darkvision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Darkvision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," -1\n"]},{"t